<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan cotton rates close up on mill demand.</title>
<headline>Pakistan cotton rates close up on mill demand.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistani cotton rates closed up on Tuesday on buying by spinners and were likely to stay firm on Wednesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Spinners were mainly buying Sindh NIAB-78 cotton, which has a quality edge over Punjab cotton in the market, broker Nasim Usman said. P compared to Monday's 2,125.</p>
</text>
